## Why This Is Asked
This checks understanding of test isolation and determinism in E2E tests using mocks for external services.

## Key Concepts
- Data seeding and reset for repeatable tests
- Network interception and mocked APIs
- End-to-end flow verification and backend validation
- CI reliability and speed trade-offs

## Code Example
```javascript
// Playwright test sketch
test('checkout end-to-end', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.route('**/payments', route => route.fulfill({ status: 200, body: JSON.stringify({ status:'success', id:'PAY123' }) }));
  await page.request.post('https://test.api/reset-db', { data: { seed: 'default' } });
  await page.goto('https://shop.example.com/product/1');
  await page.click('text=Add to cart');
  await page.goto('https://shop.example.com/checkout');
  await page.fill('#name', 'Test User');
  await page.fill('#address', '123 Main St');
  await page.click('text=Pay');
  await page.locator('text=Order Confirmed').waitFor();
  // backend verification
  const res = await page.request.get('https://test.api/orders/123');
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt this test for a flaky payment API?
- What metrics would you collect to monitor CI stability for this flow?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests RBAC in a realistic multi-tenant admin UI with progressive permission changes, ensuring isolation and correct UI cues.

## Key Concepts
- RBAC policies per-tenant
- Test data seeding and isolation
- UI visibility vs. API enforcement
- Role upgrade propagation without relogin

## Code Example
```javascript
// Playwright example sketch
test('RBAC per-tenant role upgrade', async ({ page }) => {
  await loginAsTenantUser(page, 'TenantA', 'u1', 'viewer');
  await expect(page).toHaveURL(/dashboard/);
  await expect(page.locator('#user-management')).toBeHidden();
  await upgradeRole(page, 'TenantA', 'u1', 'editor');
  await page.reload();
  await expect(page.locator('#user-management')).toBeVisible();
  await loginAsTenantUser(page, 'TenantB', 'u2', 'viewer');
  await expect(page.locator('#tenant-data')).toHaveText(/TenantA/).toBeHidden();
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle flaky network affecting role-change propagation? 
- What assertions would you add to guard against stale caches after role changes?

